      "content": "What you are feeling makes profound sense; wanting the pain to stop when someone you love is gone is a deeply human response to unbearable grief. It is not a sign of losing your mind, but rather a clear indication of how much love and how large the void he left behind is. Sometimes, the only way to manage the crushing weight of sorrow is to find tiny moments of profound rest or gentleness. Please be as kind to yourself during this exhaustion as you would be to a dear friend going through this.",
